      "math_academy_id": "q-213106",
      "sequence_position": 2,
      "problem": "Consider the following relation over the sets $A=\\{-2,-1,1,2\\}$ and $B=\\{5,7,9\\}.$ \n\n$$\nR=\\{(-2,5),(1,5),(1,7),(2,7)\\}\n$$\n\nWhat are the domain and range of this relation?\n\nThe domain is {{field-1}}\n\nThe range is {{field-2}}",
      "worked_solution": "Given a relation $R⊆A\\times B,$ \n\n- the *domain* of $R$ is the set containing all elements from $A$ that appear as the first component of the ordered pairs in $R,$ and\n\n- the *range* of $R$ is the set containing all elements from $B$ that appear as the second component of the ordered pairs in $R.$\n\nWith that in mind, we examine the given relation.\n\n- Let's consider the first components of the pairs belonging to our relation:\n\n$$\nR=\\{(-2,5),(1,5),(1,7),(2,7)\\}\n$$\n\nThe set of first components is $\\{-2,1,1,2\\}=\\{-2,1,2\\}.$ \nHence, the domain is $\\{-2,1,2\\}.$\n\n- Let's consider the second components of the pairs belonging to our relation:\n\n$$\nR=\\{(-2,5),(1,5),(1,7),(2,7)\\}\n$$\n\nThe set of second components is $\\{5,5,7,7\\}=\\{5,7\\}.$ \nHence, the range is $\\{5,7\\}.$",
